    "result_text": "Only one test file exists, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented rejection of a future `registrationDate` on `POST /api/owners` with a 400 response.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate.java`: a small single-responsibility step that reads the already-validated body (`@Val OwnerFieldsDto`) and, when a `registrationDate` is supplied and later than `LocalDate.now()`, throws the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` naming `registrationDate`. An absent date is left alone (it defaults to the server date downstream).\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted a `validateRegistrationDate` step between `validatePostcode` and `unique`, so the check sits with the other field validations and runs before any entity is built or persisted.\n\n**Reuse** \u2014 I deliberately reused the existing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` and its escalation handler (already mapped to 400) rather than adding a new exception, and kept the future-date check out of `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate` (which stays focused on resolving/weekend-adjusting the date) to avoid mixing validation into it.\n\nThe acceptance test `errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `2999-01-01`) now returns 400, and the full suite passes.",
